    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37384" root="كيأ and كوأ" body-key="k">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اكاءه</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِكَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِكَآءَةٌ</span>, <i>He came upon
him suddenly, when he</i> (the latter) <i>was about to
do a thing, and caused him to abstain from it
through fear</i> or <i>cowardice.</i> (K, TA.) But
some say that this is correctly <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكَأَهُ</span>; like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتَبَ</span>,
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِتَابٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِتَابَةٌ</span>. (TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكأ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See 1.

